      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, it also works on `native_posix` and their 64 bit flavors. It should work on both `host` toolchain and `llvm`, but for me only `llvm` worked. I\u0027ve investigated if it\u0027s possible to run our tests with ASAN, but the trick is that it needs environment variable `ASAN_OPTIONS\u003d\"log_path\u003dstdout\"`, to print errors. That\u0027s why they added the `--enable-asan` option (which basically sets `CONFIG_ASAN\u003dy` during build and `ASAN_OPTIONS` during runtime) to `twister`. IMHO, it would be better if we could just enable ASAN on specific tests.",
